Industrial-Level Python String Methods Assignment

Course: Python Programming
Level: Intermediate to Advanced (Industry-Oriented)
Topic: Python String Methods
Marks: 100
Duration: 1 Week

Scenario

You have joined a software company as a Python Developer. Your task is to develop different modules that process customer data, log files, emails, product descriptions, usernames, passwords, and reports using Python String methods.

Rules

Use only Python.
Do not use AI-generated solutions.
Every task must use the specified string methods.
Write clean and commented code.
Submit screenshots of outputs.
Use functions wherever possible.
Task 1: Employee Registration System (10 Marks)

A company stores employee names entered by HR.

Sample Input
employee = "   muhammad ali khan   "
Requirements

Use the following methods:

strip()
title()
upper()
lower()
capitalize()
Expected Output
Original:
"   muhammad ali khan   "

After strip:
muhammad ali khan

Title:
Muhammad Ali Khan

Upper:
MUHAMMAD ALI KHAN

Lower:
muhammad ali khan

Capitalize:
Muhammad ali khan
